\$$2mm]

Since the conditional distribution does not depend on the past,
\[
p(\tilde e_t\mid y_{1:t-1})
=
p(\tilde e_t),
$$
and therefore
$$
\boxed{
\tilde e_t\perp y_{1:t-1}.
}
$$

Hence $\tilde e_t$ is independent of all previous innovations.
Therefore the standardized innovations are independent across time.
\\
