\textbf{\textcolor{red}{1. The common starting point: the likelihood}}

\emph{Identifiability.} If two distinct parameter values $\phi_1\neq\phi_2$ generate exactly the same distribution for every possible dataset,
$$
p(y\mid\phi_1)=p(y\mid\phi_2)
\qquad\text{for every }y,
$$
then the model is \emph{not identifiable}: the data cannot distinguish $\phi_1$ from $\phi_2$.

